course: dictionary
lesson: 8110
title: Rental: paying to use something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rental is something you pay to use for a time, but you do not own it. A rental car, a rental flat and a bike rental all work this way: you hire them and give them back.
explain: Rental can also mean the money you pay for this, or the act of renting. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. In «rental car», rental is a describing word, so it is an adjective that tells you what sort of car it is.
explain: Some sentences have extra clues. «A rental deposit is money held in case of damage, and it comes back if the home is left in good condition.» A deposit is not the rent itself. It is kept safe, and you get it back if you look after the home. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A rental is something you pay to use for a time, but you do not own.
fact: Rental can mean the money you pay, or the act of renting.
fact: «Rental deposit» means money held in case of damage, and it comes back if the home is left in good condition.
fact: In French, «la location» means rental or hire, and «location de vélos» means bike hire.
fact: In the UK, it is illegal to ride a private e-scooter on public roads and pavements; only rental scooters in trial areas are allowed, and only for older riders with a driving licence.
exercise: Mum says «We booked a rental car for the holiday.» What is a rental? | Something you own forever | A map of the roads | A kind of holiday food | *Something you pay to use for a time but do not own
exercise: «A rental deposit is money held in case of damage.» What happens to the deposit if the home is left in good condition? | It goes to the owner's car | It is lost forever | It doubles | *It comes back
exercise: The French words «location de vélos» mean what in English? | Bike race | Bike repair | *Bike hire | Bike lights
test: A bike costs 4 pounds per hour to rent. How much does it cost to rent it for 3 hours? | *12 pounds | 7 pounds | 34 pounds | 43 pounds
test: Which phrase shows rental as the money you pay? | Rental bike | *Monthly rental payment | Rental flat | Rental car
exam: What is a rental deposit for? | To pay the owner's taxes | *To be held in case of damage | To pay for a holiday | To buy the home
